From e3744f4166480bd9204683ad9d33d2eba4d1fad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:20:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] exl3: mul1 decode window forms (tf_exl3_grouped_2_nt4 / _k6r8
 / _k8r8 / _k8r8s / _k8r16s / _k8r8p / _k8r16p)

Decode windows of a mul1 layer (GLM-5.3-Derisked-EXL3-4bpw's 4-bit routed experts; EXLR8 v0.7's mul1_e4m3 in the e4m3
image) always took tf_exl3_grouped_2 at 8 tiles a block: tilesFor sent every codebook but mcg there. The faster forms
(read-once loads, dependent launches, the one-width 8-row and the 4-tile forms) are the same grouped bodies at CB 1;
this patch instantiates them at CB 2 and tilesFor picks them for mul1 layers by the same rules as mcg's. Each gives
tf_exl3_grouped_2's bits (same k slices, MMA chains and warp-order sums). TF_EXL3_MUL1_DECODE=0 keeps
tf_exl3_grouped_2. mcg's kernels and choices are unchanged.

Checks (spark6, GB10, sm_121; the GPU shared with another workload):
  tf-cuda-test exl3-mul1-decode (new): runSlots on a 4-bit mul1 layer (top-8 of 288, D 4096, N 1024) at 1, 2, 3, 4,
    8, 9, 16 and 32 rows through each form (TF_EXL3_SHFL / TF_EXL3_PDL on, PDL off, SHFL off) and 3-bit k6r8 to 8
    rows: 30/30 byte-equal to tf_exl3_grouped_2; control: the same words on mcg give other bytes. Median time against
    tf_exl3_grouped_2: 1 row 0.242 / 0.264 ms (1.09x), 2 rows 1.06x, 4 rows 1.03x, 8 rows 1.01x, 16 rows 0.98x,
    32 rows 1.00x.
  test-glm-exl3-host 24/24.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
